  "summary": "CoreCoder is a minimal, MIT-licensed Python coding-agent engine (~1,171-line engine, 2,398 total lines) published on PyPI, featuring a bounded agent loop, eight built-in tools, consent-gated mutating tools, three-tier context compaction, sessions, plan mode, hooks, and an MCP stdio client. All claims below are product/runtime statements from the README; contributor-instruction claims were omitted per correction. Evidence coverage: 134 of 140 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
